# Line endings, which matter here more than usual: half of this repo is checked
# out on a Windows box in the plant and half is copied to a Linux server.

* text=auto

# cmd.exe is the one interpreter that genuinely minds. A .bat with bare LFs can
# mis-parse a parenthesised block or a `for` loop -- and it does it silently,
# running some of the lines. Force CRLF whatever the clone's autocrlf says.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# And the mirror image: rollup_attendance.sh is checked out here and copied to
# the application server. bash reads a trailing CR as part of the command and
# fails with "$'\r': command not found", which reads as a corrupt file.
*.sh text eol=lf
